<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<wodefinitions>
	<wo class="ERXWOComponentInstance" content="allowed" unknownAttributes="passthrough">

		<doc><![CDATA[Embeds an already constructed component instance. Where `<wo:MyComponent>` (and `WOSwitchComponent`) construct the component themselves by name - leaving bindings as the only way to initialize it and giving you no handle to it - this element takes the instance from you: construct it (`ERXComponentUtilities.instantiate(MyComponent.class, context())`), configure it, keep a reference, call methods on it, and bind it to `instance`.

```html
<wo:ERXWOComponentInstance instance="$inspector" selectedObject="$object">
  ...optional wrapped content, rendered by the instance's <wo:content />...
</wo:ERXWOComponentInstance>
```

Every other attribute is passed to the instance as a binding, exactly as on a normally embedded component. The instance is registered as a subcomponent of the page on first render, so it survives across requests (page cache, back button) like any embedded component. The binding is evaluated on every phase: bind a different instance and it is adopted immediately, the old one dropped from the page.

Rules, enforced with an exception: `instance` must not evaluate to null; the instance must not be stateless (stateless instances are pooled and shared); an instance already embedded in another parent is refused. Construct with `ERXComponentUtilities.instantiate()`, not `pageWithName()` - the latter awakens the instance and flags it as a page.]]></doc>

		<binding name="instance" required="true">
			<pull><type>com.webobjects.appserver.WOComponent</type></pull>
			<doc><![CDATA[The component instance to embed. Evaluated on every request-response phase; binding a different instance replaces the embedded component.]]></doc>
		</binding>

	</wo>
</wodefinitions>
